{"step_index":2338,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T05:25:52Z","thinking":"The provided code snippet reveals Parakeet's location selector, offering insights into its layout and styling configurations for different positions. Specifically, the \"locations\" array defines the visual characteristics (layout and corner classes) associated with each of the six slots. This should provide the necessary details.\n\n\nThe Electron window initialization uses fixed dimensions that would not allow for full-screen display. Investigation of Parakeet's window management reveals the application sets window bounds to the primary display's work area, effectively covering the entire screen. The `transparent: true` setting renders the window invisible, enabling the HTML content to be displayed as a screen overlay within the full-screen bounds.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$js = '\nconst fs = require(\"fs\");\nconst content = fs.readFileSync(\"C:/Users/Arthur Henrique/AppData/Local/Programs/parakeetai-desktop/main.js\", \"utf8\");\n\nconst idx = content.indexOf(\"renderer/set-ignore-mouse-events\");\nif (idx !== -1) {\n    console.log(content.substring(Math.max(0, idx - 100), Math.min(content.length, idx + 400)));\n}\n'\nSet-Content find_ignore_mouse_main.js $js\nnode find_ignore_mouse_main.js","Cwd":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Finding set-ignore-mouse-events in main.js","toolSummary":"Find ignore mouse in main.js"}}]}
