{"step_index":2340,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T05:26:04Z","thinking":"The code snippet directly controls whether mouse events are ignored by the main window.  The core logic `mainWindow.setIgnoreMouseEvents(t, { forward: true })` toggles click-through behavior based on the boolean value `t`. When `t` is `true`, clicks pass through; when `t` is `false`, the window intercepts clicks. This suggests the intent is to control the window's click-through transparency.\n\n\nThe renderer uses mouse events to control the click-through behavior, setting the flag to true for transparent regions and false for interactive elements. Activating the \"Move\" function, triggered by a button in the header, overlays the screen with a semi-transparent layer containing six drop zones, each representing a possible new position for the window. These zones are interactive, allowing the user to select a new location for the window.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra\\web\\index.html","EndLine":60,"StartLine":15,"toolAction":"Viewing web/index.html header structure","toolSummary":"View web/index.html header"}}]}
